###############################################################################
#  KnowGridFlow / EOIP — ASG (Application Security Group) file TEMPLATE
#
#  The real file is NEVER committed (FT-F01). Keep it in the secret store, mount
#  it read-only (chmod 400; Kubernetes Secret defaultMode 0400) and point the API
#  at it with:   EOIP_ASG_FILE=/run/secrets/eoip-asg
#
#  Entries store the SHA-256 digest of each bearer token, never the token:
#      sha256:<64 hex> | <role[,role...]> | <tenant | *> | <username>
#
#  Roles: superadmin (cross-tenant; implies admin + system), admin, system,
#         steward, analyst, viewer. Non-superadmins are tenant-bound.
#
#  Generate a token (>= 32 chars) and its digest without echoing it, e.g.:
#      python -c "import secrets;print('eoip_pat_'+secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"   # store in the password manager
#      python -c "import getpass,hashlib;print('sha256:'+hashlib.sha256(getpass.getpass().encode()).hexdigest())"
#
#  Startup fails closed when the file is missing, group/world accessible,
#  malformed, contains plaintext tokens (outside EOIP_ENV=dev with
#  EOIP_ASG_ALLOW_PLAINTEXT=true) or a digest listed in
#  EOIP_REVOKED_TOKEN_SHA256_FILE.
###############################################################################

# sha256:<hex> | superadmin | *       | root-superadmin
# sha256:<hex> | admin      | default | default-admin
# sha256:<hex> | steward    | default | data-steward
# sha256:<hex> | analyst    | default | analyst
# sha256:<hex> | viewer     | default | viewer
